cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Run It, Then Route It: Execution-Based Routing Between Small and Large LLMs for Text-to-SQL"
authors:
  - family-names: Shilman
    given-names: Andrew
    affiliation: San José State University
  - family-names: Cho
    given-names: David
    affiliation: San José State University
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ashilman25/text2sql-router"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A small local LLM answers every text-to-SQL question first. A classifier then
  predicts whether that answer is wrong from signals available only after its SQL
  has run (whether it executed, what it returned, token log-probabilities and
  agreement across samples), and only the flagged questions go to a larger model.
  Evaluated on BIRD Mini-Dev and on 68 BIRD databases unseen in training.
keywords:
  - text-to-SQL
  - LLM routing
  - model cascade
  - BIRD benchmark
  - uncertainty estimation
